# Play ViZDoom BASIC

Kill the red monster before the episode times out.

You are in a rectangular gray room. You start along one long wall, and one red
monster is placed somewhere along the opposite wall. One accurate hit kills
it. Shooting costs reward, and waiting also costs reward, so aim before firing.

Use the ViZDoom MCP tools to interact with the episode:

- Call `get_current_state` first. It returns the current screen, valid button
  names, and episode metadata.
- Before every `make_action`, write a visible note of at most 60 words with
  `Situation:` describing relevant visual facts and `Decision:` stating the
  immediate goal, selected buttons, repetition count, and expected result.
- Pass the same note to `make_action` as this JSON object:
  `{"buttons": [...], "repeat": 1, "situation": "...", "decision": "..."}`.
  Although `situation` and `decision` are optional in the tool schema for
  compatibility, you must always supply both. You may press multiple buttons
  together; an empty list waits. `repeat` may be 1-8, and each repetition
  advances four frames.
- Make only one `make_action` call per tool invocation. Use `repeat` for a short
  coherent action sequence, then inspect the returned state and screen before
  deciding again. Do not run loops that call `make_action` repeatedly from one
  observation.

The available buttons are `MOVE_LEFT`, `MOVE_RIGHT`, and `ATTACK`. Continue
until a tool result reports `done: true`. Success means the monster was killed;
a timeout is failure.

Do not use the internet or access the game by any route other than the
provided ViZDoom MCP tools. Built-in web search and web fetch are disabled.
